  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Generics Exist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What A Generic Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A type parameterized by another type.",
            "A function from types to types.",
            "Evaluated by tsc only, never at runtime."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Where `any` Breaks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function identity(x: any): any {",
            "  return x  // link input->output lost",
            "}",
            "identity(5).toUpperCase()  // compiles!",
            "// TypeError at runtime, not compile time"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`any` erases the input/output relation.",
            "Overloads: one signature per type, forever.",
            "Overloads never cover user-defined types."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Repair"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function identity<T>(x: T): T {",
            "  return x  // T binds both positions",
            "}",
            "identity(5).toUpperCase()  // Error, caught"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Generics buy relational typing.",
            "They say two positions are the same type.",
            "`any` and `unknown` cannot say that.",
            "Type in 2+ positions? generic. In 1? drop it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Erasure Is Total"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Emitted JS has no T, no type argument.",
            "`typeof T` is not a thing.",
            "No `new T()`, no `x instanceof T`.",
            "Cannot branch on a type parameter at runtime."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Pass A Value Instead",
          "text": "Erased type info returns as runtime data: a constructor, a string tag, or a schema object."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Declaring Parameters"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "class Box<T> { v!: T }",
            "interface Pair<A, B> { a: A; b: B }",
            "type Result<T, E> = { ok: T } | { err: E }",
            "const id = <T,>(x: T) => x  // ',' for .tsx"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "class Stack<T> {",
            "  #items: T[] = []",
            "  push(x: T) { this.#items.push(x) }",
            "  pop() { return this.#items.pop() }",
            "}  // new Stack<number>() or inferred"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function Ser<B extends Ctor<object>>(Base: B) {",
            "  return class extends Base {",
            "    toJSON() { return { ...this } }",
            "  }  // return type keeps Base's shape",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Push<T extends unknown[], V> = [...T, V]",
            "type Cat<A extends unknown[],",
            "  B extends unknown[]> = [...A, ...B]",
            "// variadic tuples pair with infer"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Aw<T> = T extends {",
            "  then(cb: (v: infer V) => any): any",
            "} ? Aw<V> : T",
            "// Promise<Promise<string>> -> string"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Equal<A, B> =",
            "  (<T>() => T extends A ? 1 : 2) extends",
            "  (<T>() => T extends B ? 1 : 2)",
            "    ? true : false  // strict equality trick"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Why Generics Exist (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Scope And Naming",
          "items": [
            "Visible: signature, body, nested types.",
            "Invisible inside `static` class members.",
            "T lone; K key, V value, E elem/error, R return.",
            "P props; TItem/TKey for multi-param APIs."
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Order And Arity"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Map<K, V>",
              "ordered, positional"
            ],
            [
              "Map<V, K>",
              "a different type"
            ],
            [
              "Pair<string>",
              "needs 2 type args"
            ],
            [
              "bare `Box`",
              "alias must be applied"
            ],
            [
              "bare `<T>`",
              "bounded by unknown"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Read It Aloud",
          "text": "pluck<T, K extends keyof T>(items: T[], key: K): T[K][] — for any T and any key K of T, map T[] to the values at K."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Inference At The Call Site",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`identity('hi')` infers T = string, no args.",
            "Explicit args are an override, not a duty.",
            "tsc collects candidates by structural match.",
            "Then picks the best common supertype."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Conflicting Candidates"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function pair<T>(a: T, b: T): T[] {",
            "  return [a, b]",
            "}",
            "pair(1, 'x')  // T = string | number"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inference widens to a union, it does not error.",
            "Return and contextual sites rank lower.",
            "An earlier concrete argument wins conflicts.",
            "No candidate? falls back to constraint or unknown."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Widening And `const` T"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "T becomes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "identity('hi')",
              "string"
            ],
            [
              "identity<'hi'>('hi')",
              "'hi'"
            ],
            [
              "f(['a','b'])",
              "string[]"
            ],
            [
              "const T, same call",
              "readonly ['a','b']"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Constraints change widening: `T extends string` keeps literals.",
            "`const T` (TS 5.0) kills caller-side `as const`.",
            "Contextual types flow inward: `arr.map(x => x.length)`.",
            "An unused parameter silently becomes unknown."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function first<T>(a: readonly T[]) {",
            "  return a[0]  // T | undefined",
            "}",
            "// plain T[] would reject readonly arrays"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Inference And Constraints",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "No Partial Application",
          "text": "Supply one of two type args and you must supply both. Workaround: curry — builder<Schema>() returns a generic function that infers the rest."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. `extends` As A Bound"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Restricts what the caller may pass in.",
            "Grants the body the bound's members.",
            "That two-sided bargain is the whole trade.",
            "Means 'assignable to', not class inheritance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function len<T extends { length: number }>(",
            "  x: T",
            ") { return x.length }  // body may read it",
            "len('abc'); len([1, 2])  // both fit bound"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Common bound",
            "Admits"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "T extends object",
              "non-primitives"
            ],
            [
              "K extends keyof U",
              "one key of U"
            ],
            [
              "T extends unknown[]",
              "tuples, arrays"
            ],
            [
              "(...a: any[]) => any",
              "any function"
            ],
            [
              "abstract new (...a)",
              "constructors"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Constraint Gotchas"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "F-bounded: `<T extends Comparable<T>>` — self-comparable.",
            "Constraints see earlier params only, left to right.",
            "`<K extends keyof T, T>` is illegal, order matters.",
            "A constrained T is NOT its constraint."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function f<T extends { a: number }>(x: T) {",
            "  x = { a: 1 }  // Error: T may need more",
            "}  // read props yes, construct T no",
            "declare function get<T, K extends keyof T>(",
            "  o: T, k: K): T[K]  // rejects get({a:1},'b')"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Do Not Over-Constrain",
          "text": "`<T extends string>(x: T): string` throws T away on the way out. Return T and the caller keeps the literal type."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. `keyof` Basics",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Expression",
            "Yields"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "keyof {a:1,b:2}",
              "'a' | 'b'"
            ],
            [
              "keyof any",
              "string|number|symbol"
            ],
            [
              "keyof (A | B)",
              "keyof A & keyof B"
            ],
            [
              "keyof Record<string,n>",
              "string | number"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Keys, Classes, Containers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Union of the type's public property keys.",
            "Unions intersect: only shared keys are safe.",
            "Index signatures widen keyof, numerics coerce.",
            "So Record lookups return V for missing keys."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Indexed Access"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type N = Person['name']    // property type",
            "type Vals = T[keyof T]     // all value types",
            "type El = Items[number]    // element type",
            "type Color = typeof COLORS[number]  // union"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`keyof` an array adds every Array.prototype member.",
            "Want elements? use `T[number]` instead.",
            "`T[number]` over an `as const` array is the idiom."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Turn On noUncheckedIndexedAccess",
          "text": "It adds `| undefined` to every index-signature and array read. Generic container code is exactly where that flag pays."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Key-Driven Patterns"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "declare function set<T, K extends keyof T>(",
            "  o: T, k: K, v: T[K]): void",
            "set(p, 'age', 'old')  // Error: needs number",
            "type KeysOfType<T, V> = {",
            "  [K in keyof T]-?: T[K] extends V?K:never",
            "}[keyof T]"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Value type is tied to the key type, so typos fail.",
            "`type FnKeys = KeysOfType<Window, Function>`.",
            "Extracts every method name without listing one."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Interfaces And Classes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "interface Repo<T> {",
            "  find(id: string): Promise<T | null>",
            "  save(x: T): Promise<void>",
            "}  // T bound at use site: Repo<User>"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Keys, Classes, Containers (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Alias vs Interface",
          "items": [
            "Alias: unions, conditionals, mapped, template.",
            "Interface: declaration merging, nicer errors.",
            "`static empty: T` — statics cannot see T.",
            "Methods may add their own: `map<U>(f): Box<U>`."
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Structural Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Box<string>` and `{ value: string }` interchange freely.",
            "`class Tagged<T> { id: string }` — T is invisible.",
            "So Tagged<Dog> and Tagged<Cat> are assignable.",
            "Fix with a phantom field: `private __brand?: T`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Constructors And Mixins"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Ctor<T> = new (...a: any[]) => T",
            "function create<T>(C: Ctor<T>): T {",
            "  return new C()  // value stands in for T",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Default Type Parameters",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "interface Options<T = string> { value: T }",
            "// Options === Options<string>",
            "type Pair<A, B = A> = [A, B]",
            "type P = Pair<number>   // arity fixed"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Defaults make trailing parameters optional.",
            "May reference earlier params: `<T, U = T[]>`.",
            "Never later ones — same left-to-right rule.",
            "`<T extends string = number>` errors: default must fit bound."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Default Is Not Inferred",
          "text": "A default applies only when nothing is supplied AND nothing can be inferred. Any inference candidate wins."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Explicit Arguments"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Move",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "parse<Config>(j)",
              "pins the union"
            ],
            [
              "explicit arg",
              "skips widening"
            ],
            [
              "useState<any>(x)",
              "opts out of typing"
            ],
            [
              "Promise<T = void>",
              "90% omit the arg"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Explicit args override inference entirely.",
            "They also silence the check inference would run.",
            "React's useState, createContext, reduce<U> all lean on this.",
            "Split calls to fix T then infer the rest."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "const make = builder<Schema>()  // fixes T",
            "make(value)                    // infers rest"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Defaults And Branching Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Conditional Types"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type IsString<T> = T extends string",
            "  ? true : false",
            "type A = IsString<'a'>  // true",
            "type B = IsString<1>    // false"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A compile-time ternary judged by assignability.",
            "Not by any runtime value — nothing is evaluated.",
            "Unresolved T? the conditional stays deferred and opaque.",
            "So inside a generic body it fits neither branch."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Deferred Bites Implementations",
          "text": "You usually need an internal overload, or one isolated cast at the implementation boundary, to satisfy a deferred conditional."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Type-Level Switch"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Kind<T> =",
            "  T extends string ? 'str' :",
            "  T extends number ? 'num' : 'other'",
            "// never as a branch = 'no case'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Built-in",
            "Body"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Exclude<T,U>",
              "T extends U ? never : T"
            ],
            [
              "Extract<T,U>",
              "T extends U ? T : never"
            ],
            [
              "NonNullable<T>",
              "T & {}"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`never` vanishes from unions — that is why filters work.",
            "`any` in the checked slot returns BOTH branches unioned.",
            "`never` in a distributive slot returns `never`.",
            "Recursion is legal: DeepReadonly maps itself downward."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Params<S> =",
            "  S extends `${string}:${infer P}/${infer R}`",
            "    ? P | Params<R>",
            "    : S extends `${string}:${infer P}` ? P",
            "    : never  // route parser sketch"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. `infer` Captures A Slot",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Declares a fresh variable inside `extends`.",
            "Legal in that position and nowhere else.",
            "Whatever matched there becomes the variable.",
            "Then use it in the true branch."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Ret<T> = T extends (...a: any[]) => infer R",
            "  ? R : never",
            "type Par<T> = T extends (...a: infer P) => any",
            "  ? P : never",
            "type El<T> = T extends (infer E)[] ? E : never"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Stdlib Built On infer",
          "items": [
            "ReturnType, Parameters, InstanceType.",
            "Awaited unwraps nested promises.",
            "ElementOf for array element types.",
            "All the same conditional shape."
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "infer And Distribution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Position Decides The Join"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Same name in",
            "Combines to"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "covariant slots",
              "a union"
            ],
            [
              "parameter slots",
              "an intersection"
            ],
            [
              "last overload only",
              "silent pick"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "That asymmetry is variance leaking into inference.",
            "Contravariant sites intersect the candidates.",
            "ReturnType on an overloaded function picks the last one."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Match Shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type ToNum<S> =",
            "  S extends `${infer N extends number}`",
            "    ? N : never          // TS 4.7 filter",
            "type Head<T> = T extends [infer H, ...infer R]",
            "  ? H : never            // recursion workhorse"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Distribution Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Naked type parameter + union input = per-member run.",
            "Results are re-unioned afterwards.",
            "`ToArray<string|number>` is `string[] | number[]`.",
            "NOT `(string | number)[]` — a common shock."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type ToArray<T> = T extends any ? T[] : never",
            "type Off<T> = [T] extends [any] ? T[] : never",
            "// Off<string|number> = (string|number)[]"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Checked slot",
            "Distributes?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "naked T",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "[T]",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "T[] / Foo<T>",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "keyof T",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Distribution is why Exclude<'a'|'b'|'c','a'> = 'b'|'c'.",
            "`never` is the empty union: zero branches run.",
            "So `ToArray<never>` is `never`, not `never[]`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Distribution At Work"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type EventOf<T, K> = T extends { type: K }",
            "  ? T : never",
            "type Handlers<E extends { type: string }> = {",
            "  [K in E['type']]: (e: EventOf<E, K>) => void",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "infer And Distribution (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Triage Checklist",
          "text": "Unexpected union? distribution ran. Unexpected never? a never input. Unexpected non-distribution? T was not naked."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mapping A Key Union",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Wrap<T> = { [K in keyof T]: F<T[K]> }",
            "type Required<T> = { [K in keyof T]-?: T[K] }",
            "// ? / -? optionality, readonly / -readonly"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Iterate a key union, emit a new object type.",
            "Modifiers add or strip `?` and `readonly`.",
            "`as` remaps keys (TS 4.1), including to `never`.",
            "Remapping to `never` deletes the key."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Getters<T> = {",
            "  [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<K & string>}`]:",
            "    () => T[K]",
            "}",
            "type NoFns<T> = { [K in keyof T as",
            "  T[K] extends Function ? never : K]: T[K] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Homomorphic Or Not"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Keeps"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "[K in keyof T]",
              "array, tuple, modifiers"
            ],
            [
              "[K in SomeUnion]",
              "nothing, flat object"
            ],
            [
              "Partial<string[]>",
              "still an array"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bare `keyof T` over a bare T is homomorphic.",
            "It preserves array-ness, tuple-ness, `?` and readonly.",
            "Written over a key union instead, all of that is lost."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Stdlib To Know Cold",
          "items": [
            "Partial, Required, Readonly.",
            "Record<K, V>, Pick<T, K extends keyof T>.",
            "Omit<T, K> — key is NOT checked.",
            "Omit<User,'nmae'> compiles silently."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Write StrictOmit<T, K extends keyof T> to catch typos.",
            "Add conditionals plus recursion for DeepPartial, Mutable.",
            "Same machinery builds JSON-serializability transforms."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type FormState<T> = {",
            "  [K in keyof T]: {",
            "    value: T[K]; error?: string",
            "    touched: boolean",
            "  }  // whole state from one model",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Variance Question"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Given Dog extends Animal, when is F<Dog> assignable to F<Animal>? The answer depends on where T sits."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Mapped Types And Variance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Kind",
            "Direction",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "covariant",
              "preserved",
              "readonly Animal[]"
            ],
            [
              "contravariant",
              "reversed",
              "(x: Animal) => void"
            ],
            [
              "invariant",
              "neither",
              "Array<T>, Map<K,V>"
            ],
            [
              "bivariant",
              "both",
              "method params"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Producer of Dogs is a producer of Animals.",
            "A handler taking any Animal fits where Dog handlers go.",
            "Array<Dog> as Array<Animal> would let you push a Cat.",
            "Bivariance is unsound and kept for ergonomics."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Accepted Hole"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "const dogs: Dog[] = [rex]",
            "const animals: Animal[] = dogs  // allowed",
            "animals.push(new Cat())  // dogs corrupted",
            "// arrays are unsoundly covariant, by design"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`strictFunctionTypes` makes standalone fn params contravariant.",
            "It deliberately skips method declarations.",
            "So `Array<T>.push` and DOM handlers keep working."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Derive It From Position",
          "text": "Output positions covariant, input contravariant, both invariant, neither independent. Mental model: give T, take T, or both."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Explicit Annotations",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "interface Producer<out T> { get(): T }",
            "interface Consumer<in T> { put(x: T): void }",
            "interface Store<in out T> {",
            "  get(): T; put(x: T): void",
            "}  // TS 4.7"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Checked, not asserted: a wrong mark is an error.",
            "`out T` used in a parameter slot fails to compile.",
            "So they document and guard at the same time.",
            "`in out` is the safe conservative choice."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why They Exist",
          "text": "Speed. Measuring variance structurally on big recursive generics is slow; an annotation lets the checker compare by variance instead of deep structure."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Test It Yourself"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "let a: F<Animal>; let d: F<Dog>",
            "a = d  // ok? then covariant",
            "d = a  // ok? then contravariant",
            "// both ok = bivariant, neither = invariant"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Measuring Variance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Variance in T"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "readonly T[]",
              "covariant, safe"
            ],
            [
              "T[]",
              "covariant, unsafe"
            ],
            [
              "Promise<T>",
              "covariant"
            ],
            [
              "(x: T) => void",
              "contravariant"
            ],
            [
              "Map<K, V>",
              "invariant in both"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer `readonly T[]` in parameters, soundness for free.",
            "Map is invariant because its methods mutate.",
            "Constraints do not fix variance — usage does."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Cb<T> = (cb: (x: T) => void) => void",
            "// contravariance twice cancels out:",
            "// Cb<T> is covariant in T"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Design Rule",
          "text": "Read-only containers covariant, sinks and handlers contravariant. Reach for invariance only when the type truly reads and writes."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Higher-Order Inference"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "TS 3.4: composing generics propagates free parameters.",
            "`compose(f, g)` can stay generic, not collapse to unknown.",
            "Contextual return inference kills inline annotations."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "const f: <T>(x: T) => T = x => x",
            "// x typed from the annotation alone",
            "function map<T, U>(a: T[], g: (x: T) => U): U[]",
            "// T from the array, then fed to g's param"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Priority Tiers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rank",
